    "instructions": "Practise one G bar twice, then one C bar twice, then one D bar twice. Rest for a full bar after every attempt. Count 1-and-2-and-3-and-4-and. Melody attacks stay on numbered beats; pluck the open-string fills gently on the and. Quarter-note melody attacks are now articulated as eighth-note plucks; keep the original two-beat phrase endings. Let strings ring naturally where comfortable; do not re-pluck a sustained half note. Bass uses G on low E fret 3, C on A fret 3 and open D.",
